==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|bio|electronics|lang=en}}. Coined by US Air Force [[medical doctor]] [[w:Jack E. Steele|Jack E. Steele]] in 1958 to refer to the "flow of concepts from biology to engineering and vice versa".

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈbaɪˌɒnɪks/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-}}

# The [[design]] of [[engineering]] [[system]]s, especially [[electronic]] ones, based on that of [[biological]] systems.
# [[biomimetics]]

